secureshellgo (1.4.3~noble1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Quick connect accepts a whole ssh command, of the kind a cloud console
    gives you to copy. Pasting one previously made everything before the "@"
    the username, so the server rejected an account named after the command
    itself. Quoted key paths, -p, -l, bare switches, flag values, a trailing
    remote command and ssh:// URLs are all understood.
  * Quick connect can import a .pem or other key file from disk instead of
    requiring the key to be pasted as text.
  * After a connection succeeds, quick connect offers to save the host rather
    than leaving a button to be noticed. The offer never delays the session.
  * Fixes a layout failure that left the quick connect screen showing its
    title bar over a blank page after a successful connection.

 -- Dhiva Labs <dhivakar1010@gmail.com>  Wed, 06 Aug 2026 04:10:00 +0530

